A bare thermistor has 2 legs with no polarity. Insert it into two breadboard rows. Take a
10kΩ resistor and put one leg into the same row as one of the thermistor’s legs (this creates the
shared “midpoint” node), and its other leg into an empty row. Now wire: thermistor’s other leg →
red (+) rail; resistor’s free leg → blue (−) rail; and run a jumper from the shared midpoint row →
Arduino A0.
